ay W3, Play T7, Play B8.\nThe game history of the previous player is: Play F2, Play T9, Play B8, Play F2, Play W8, Play F2, Play B2, Play F4, Play T7, Play B5, Play F1, Play B6, Play J1, Play J1, Play F4, Play T1, Play T6, Play T5, Play B7, Play T4, Play T2.\nThe followings are your valid actions:[Play T9; Play W6; Play W7; Play W3; Play W4]\u3002", "reasoning": "", "output": "Evaluation: My hand is W3, W4, W4, W6, W6, W7, W7, T9, plus two melds: Chow T3,T4,T5 and Chow T2,T3,T4. I have 9 tiles in hand, needing 4 more for a standard hand (14 tiles). But since I have two melds already (6 tiles exposed), my hand tiles count is 9, total 15? Wait, check: Two melds use 6 tiles. Hand has 5 distinct types but counts: W3(1), W4(2), W6(2), W7(2), T9(1) = 8 tiles? Actually list: [W3:1; W4:2; W6:2; W7:2; T9:1] sums to 1+2+2+2+1=8 tiles. Plus 6 from melds = 14 total. So I have a complete hand of 14 tiles? But it's not a winning hand because no pair and melds structure? Actually standard winning requires 4 melds + 1 pair. I have 2 melds exposed, and hand tiles: potentially can form more melds/pair. But currently not winning. I need to discard one tile to maintain 13 tiles (since after discard, hand tiles become 7, plus 6 from melds = 13, waiting for winning tile). So valid actions are discards: T9, W6, W7, W3, W4.\n\nI need to choose which discard improves hand towards winning. Current hand: W3, W4, W4, W6, W6, W7, W7, T9. I have many W tiles, possible to aim for Full Flush (all W) or Half Flush. But I have T9 and two T melds already exposed, so Half Flush maybe possible if I discard T9? Half Flush requires only honor tiles and one suit. I have no honors, but my exposed melds are T suits, so if I keep T9, I have T suit also. But Half Flush pattern: hand consists of only honor tiles and suited tiles of one suit. My exposed melds are T suit, so if I keep T9, my hand has W suit and T9, so not one suit. To achieve Half Flush, I would need to convert all hand tiles to T suit or honors